  "summary": "Jeanne Bliss argues that beloved companies differentiate themselves by a clear, unique promise to customers. When decisions are made, they are aligned to that purpose, elevating work from merely executing tasks to delivering memorable experiences that customers will want to repeat. These experiences are reinforced by ironclad integrity and clarity that guide every decision, especially at forks in the road where the yes button is revealed. In operations, such clarity unites the organization around the customer story and the employee story, driving extreme loyalty and business growth.",
